   "<p class=\"ui-lead\">Compare this fingerprint with the one shown on the server's console before allowing Homestead to sign in.</p><div class=\"ui-callout warn\" role=\"alert\">\n      <span class=\"ui-callout-icon\"><svg class=\"ui-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-alert\"/></svg></span>\n      <div><div class=\"ui-notice-line ui-notice-whole\"><b class=\"ui-notice-head\">Check the fingerprint on the server itself</b><span class=\"ui-notice-first ui-issue-short\">Use the server's own screen or a management session already trusted, not this new SSH connection.</span></div></div>\n    </div><dl class=\"ui-facts\"><div><dt>Host</dt><dd>192.0.2.10:22</dd></div><div><dt>Host key</dt><dd>ssh-ed25519</dd></div></dl><section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>Compare fingerprint</h4></header>\n    <div class=\"mono\" style=\"overflow-wrap:anywhere\">SHA256:fixture</div></section><section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>Command to run on the server</h4></header>\n    <code style=\"overflow-wrap:anywhere\">ssh-keygen -lf /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub</code></section><details class=\"ui-more\" data-disclosure=\"Effects of trusting this key\">\n    <summary>Effects of trusting this key</summary><div class=\"ui-more-body\"><p>New connections to this server must match this key. If the key changes, new connections stop until it is trusted again. Copies already running keep the key and credentials they started with.</p></div></details><label class=\"ui-ack\">\n    <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"sourceKeyAck\" onchange=\"sourceKeyReady()\"><span>I compared this fingerprint with the source host's console.</span></label><div class=\"ui-actions\" >\n      <div class=\"ui-actions-start\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" onclick=\"closeModal()\" data-dialog-dismiss=\"true\">Not now</button></div><div class=\"ui-actions-end\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn pri\" id=\"sourceKeyApply\" onclick=\"sourceKeyTrust()\" disabled >Trust this source</button></div></div>"
